    body_en: "Parental leave has become established as an important policy helping people balance work and family. However, in practice, voices still say it is hard to use freely. Some workers worry that taking parental leave could lead to disadvantages in promotion or evaluation. Especially at small and medium businesses, the leave usage rate is low because finding replacement staff is difficult. On the other hand, more companies have workplace cultures that actively encourage parental leave. Such companies are said to have an advantage in attracting top talent. The government is trying to boost the system through higher parental leave pay and subsidies for replacement staff. The two contrasting realities surrounding parental leave reveal the gap between policy and workplace culture.",
